# Firestore Admin SDK conventions

## Initialization

- Firestore Admin SDK must be initialized in `src/database/firestoreAdmin.js`.
- Load config from environment variables; do not hardcode credentials.
- Expose a `getDb()` function returning a singleton Firestore instance.

## Repositories

- Put persistence functions in `src/database/repos/**`.
- Repos should export small, focused functions (e.g. `getUserById`, `createUser`).
- Repos must not contain business logic; only CRUD + query composition.

## Services

- Services call repos and implement business rules (e.g. uniqueness, normalization).
- Controllers never call repos directly.

